indings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"No-id same-content events collide and are skipped as duplicates\",\"evidence\":\"Tech design line 329 requires fallback idempotency keys to be identical for re-delivery of the same logical event and distinct across different events, using a role/timestamp/content-hash fallback. The implemented fallback in packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts:37-57 omits timestamp/source order and uses only blockIndex, role, kind, and content. Production hook routing in packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts:348-354 calls mapMessage with only piSessionId, and local MessageEndEvent in packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts:36-38 carries only message, so messages without embedded entryId use the content-only fallback. Runtime changes in packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/runtime-changes.ts:38-48 also use the same content-only fallback. LHC skips duplicate idempotency keys in packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts:210-216. A focused production-path node run through createConnector recorded two identical user prompts separated by agent_end as only [\\\"user_prompt\\\",\\\"turn_end\\\"] with eventCount 2, proving the second finalized message and its turn_end were skipped instead of recorded.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/idempotency.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/map-message.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/runtime-changes.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/capture/turn-accumulator.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/index.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/src/pi/types.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/idempotency.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/reattach-idempotency.test.ts\",\"packages/pi-lhc/test/capture/converter.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.1\",\"AC-2.6\",\"AC-2.8\",\"TC-2.7\",\"TC-2.9\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"No-id same-content events collide and are skipped as duplicates\",\"evidence\":\"Tec